ta-transcript-engine-root="" class="contents"><div data-cds="Prose" class="prose stacks:[&amp;_li:not(:where([data-cds-theme],[data-cds-theme]_*))::marker]:[--cds-text-secondary:var(--cds-text-primary)]" style="--_prose-font-body: var(--font-claude-response, var(--cds-font-voice)); --_prose-font-heading-display: var(--_prose-font-heading);"><div data-perf-reply-text="" class="_blocks_4za3l_47 standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 whitespace-normal break-words print:block"><p dir="ltr">Iâ€™ve made the change: before login visitors see the full promotional page, and after login they see only the tasks, the map and the tools. Your screenshot still shows the older header (Browse tasks, Conversations, Sign up and so on), so the last version never reached GitHub. This new file includes it as well.</p>
<p dir="ltr" data-cds-heading=""><strong>What changes after login</strong></p>
<ul dir="ltr">
<li>The hero, â€œConversationsâ€, â€œHow it worksâ€, â€œTrustâ€, the call-to-action and Terms sections all disappear.</li>
<li>The page opens straight on a greeting such as â€œHi Darsh ðŸ‘‹ What do you need done today?â€, with buttons for Post a task, My tasks, My offers and Notifications.</li>
<li>The task list and map follow, as they are now.</li>
<li>How it works, Trust &amp; safety and Terms are still in the â˜° menu and the footer. They open as pop-up windows instead of page sections.</li>
<li>Logging out brings the full promotional page back.</li>
<li>Returning users donâ€™t see the promotional page flash before it hides.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="ltr"><strong>Update with one file instead of three</strong><br>
I put the HTML, styling and code into a single file, so you only upload and rename once. Your phone downloaded <code dir="ltr">.txt</code> files before, so I kept that format.</p>
<ol dir="ltr">
<li>Download <code dir="ltr">index-html.txt</code>.</li>
<li>On GitHub: <strong>Add file â†’ Upload files</strong> â†’ pick <code dir="ltr">index-html.txt</code> â†’ <strong>Commit changes</strong>.</li>
<li>Tap <code dir="ltr">index.html</code> in the repo â†’ <strong>â‹¯</strong> â†’ <strong>Delete file</strong> â†’ <strong>Commit</strong>.</li>
<li>Tap <code dir="ltr">index-html.txt</code> â†’ pencil (Edit) â†’ change the name to <code dir="ltr">index.html</code> â†’ <strong>Commit changes</strong>.</li>
<li>Wait a minute or two, then hard-refresh.</li>
</ol>
<p dir="ltr">Leave <code dir="ltr">app.js</code>, <code dir="ltr">styles.css</code> and <code dir="ltr">airtasker.css</code> in the repo; the new <code dir="ltr">index.html</code> no longer uses them. Keep <code dir="ltr">supabase-config.js</code>.</p>
<p dir="ltr"><strong>Something to check in your data</strong><br>
Both of your tasks now show â€œArea not specifiedâ€, where they used to show Eldoret. Iâ€™m not sure why, so <code dir="ltr">05-safe-coords-trigger.sql</code> does two things: it rebuilds the coordinate trigger so it only touches coordinate columns, and it shows your tasks and their saved areas. Paste the whole file into the Supabase SQL Editor and run it. If the <code dir="ltr">location</code> column is empty for those tasks, remove the two dashes in front of the last <code dir="ltr">update</code> line, change the town if needed, and run it again.</p>
<p dir="ltr">I tested the new logic with stand-ins, not in a live browser, so please check the logged-in view on your phone.</p>
<p dir="ltr">Files are in the outputs:</p>
<ul dir="ltr">
<li>index-html.txt</li>
<li>05-safe-coords-trigger.sql</li>
